{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-glaucoma-what-it-is/audio/main-b42958ec8f29.mp3","durationSec":268.992,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.64,"text":"Imagine some people at an eye test."},{"start":2.18,"end":2.94,"text":"They all feel fine."},{"start":3.48,"end":5.54,"text":"They can see well, and they have no pain."},{"start":6.18,"end":8.34,"text":"But one of them already has early glaucoma."},{"start":8.88,"end":9.74,"text":"How is this possible?"},{"start":10.46,"end":13.28,"text":"To answer this, we need to know about the optic nerve."},{"start":13.94,"end":16.92,"text":"This is the main nerve that connects the eye to the brain."},{"start":17.8,"end":19.46,"text":"Think of a TV camera and a screen."},{"start":20.18,"end":21.44,"text":"The eye is like the camera."},{"start":21.78,"end":23,"text":"The brain is like the screen."},{"start":23.68,"end":25.72,"text":"The optic nerve is the cable between them."},{"start":26.54,"end":31.72,"text":"If the cable is damaged, the picture cannot reach the screen, even when the camera works perfectly."},{"start":32.58,"end":34.04,"text":"Glaucoma damages this cable."},{"start":34.74,"end":39.56,"text":"Often the damage starts quietly, so a person can have glaucoma and still feel normal."},{"start":40.48,"end":43.04,"text":"Feeling fine is not the same as being fine."},{"start":44.36,"end":45.84,"text":"Why does the optic nerve get damaged?"},{"start":46.7,"end":48.48,"text":"Usually, the problem is fluid."},{"start":49.26,"end":52.88,"text":"There is fluid inside the eye, and it needs to drain out properly."},{"start":53.56,"end":55.2,"text":"Think of a kitchen sink with the tap on."},{"start":55.2,"end":59.06,"text":"If the drain works, the water goes away and the sink never fills up."},{"start":59.58,"end":61.68,"text":"But if the drain is slow, the water rises."},{"start":63.02,"end":66.56,"text":"In the eye, the fluid cannot drain properly, so eye pressure goes up."},{"start":67.46,"end":70.6,"text":"This high pressure pushes on the optic nerve and damages it."},{"start":71.04,"end":73.16,"text":"But the story is not always so simple."},{"start":73.9,"end":77.42,"text":"Sometimes the optic nerve is damaged even when eye pressure is normal."},{"start":77.94,"end":81.34,"text":"So high pressure is the usual cause, but it is not the only one."},{"start":81.9,"end":83.38,"text":"This is important for the next parts."},{"start":83.9,"end":87.1,"text":"A normal pressure number does not always mean a healthy nerve."},{"start":88.44,"end":91.1,"text":"Most of the time, glaucoma gives no early warning."},{"start":92.02,"end":95.6,"text":"Many people find out at a routine eye test, before they notice any problem."},{"start":96.16,"end":98.32,"text":"This is why it can be called a quiet problem."},{"start":98.96,"end":102.28,"text":"However, glaucoma can sometimes come suddenly."},{"start":102.96,"end":105.84,"text":"Then the symptoms are very clear:\n\nintense eye pain."},{"start":107.46,"end":108.18,"text":"a red eye."},{"start":108.18,"end":112.08,"text":"rainbow-coloured circles around lights."},{"start":112.08,"end":113.32,"text":"blurred vision."},{"start":114.62,"end":115.06,"text":"nausea."},{"start":116.12,"end":116.56,"text":"a headache."},{"start":117.78,"end":119.3,"text":"This sudden type is an emergency."},{"start":120,"end":121.64,"text":"The person needs treatment immediately."},{"start":122.26,"end":124.06,"text":"They should not wait for a normal appointment."},{"start":124.78,"end":126.52,"text":"So glaucoma can be very different."},{"start":127.2,"end":130.44,"text":"Usually it is quiet, and only a check can find it."},{"start":130.96,"end":134.42,"text":"Sometimes it is loud and sudden, and it needs help at once."},{"start":135.56,"end":139.12,"text":"If glaucoma is often quiet, how do doctors find it?"},{"start":139.84,"end":142.8,"text":"Very often, it is found during a routine eye test."},{"start":143.4,"end":146.28,"text":"This is a normal check, not a visit because of a problem."},{"start":146.82,"end":148.56,"text":"The person may feel completely fine."},{"start":149.28,"end":153.74,"text":"When the eye tester sees possible signs of glaucoma, the patient is referred to a specialist."},{"start":154.58,"end":157.62,"text":"The specialist then does further tests to look more closely."},{"start":158.34,"end":159.48,"text":"Why are more tests needed?"},{"start":160.32,"end":162.12,"text":"Remember Part 2."},{"start":162.12,"end":164.66,"text":"Damage can happen even when eye pressure is normal."},{"start":165.12,"end":167.98,"text":"So one number alone cannot tell the whole story."},{"start":167.98,"end":171.1,"text":"Doctors need to look at the eye in more than one way."},{"start":171.92,"end":174.4,"text":"Remember the person in Part 1 who \"felt fine\"."},{"start":175,"end":177.46,"text":"They can only find out about their glaucoma at a check."},{"start":178.2,"end":180.78,"text":"Waiting for symptoms often means waiting too long."},{"start":180.78,"end":184.84,"text":"Doctors treat glaucoma with eye drops, laser treatment and surgery."},{"start":185.7,"end":189.24,"text":"Eye drops, laser treatment and surgery all have the same goal."},{"start":189.74,"end":191.72,"text":"They reduce the fluid and pressure in the eye."},{"start":192.38,"end":193.3,"text":"Think of the sink again."},{"start":193.92,"end":197.18,"text":"Treatment helps the water go down, so it stops pressing so hard."},{"start":197.98,"end":200.36,"text":"But we must be honest about what treatment can do."},{"start":200.86,"end":201.88,"text":"It can slow the damage."},{"start":202.4,"end":204,"text":"It can stop vision from getting worse."},{"start":204.66,"end":208.44,"text":"It cannot cure glaucoma, and it cannot bring back sight that is already lost."},{"start":209.2,"end":211.4,"text":"A damaged cable does not repair itself."},{"start":212.6,"end":214.74,"text":"This is why regular follow-ups are important."},{"start":214.74,"end":218.1,"text":"Doctors use them to check that the treatment is really working."},{"start":218.56,"end":219.98,"text":"Treatment is not a single day."},{"start":220.62,"end":222.08,"text":"It is a long-term job."},{"start":222.72,"end":227.08,"text":"If treatment only protects the sight you still have, then timing matters."},{"start":227.96,"end":230,"text":"The patient has an important role here."},{"start":230.42,"end":234.52,"text":"First, people with glaucoma should use their eye drops every day."},{"start":234.52,"end":237.24,"text":"Drops only work when they are used."},{"start":237.72,"end":240.16,"text":"A day without drops is a day without protection."},{"start":240.96,"end":242.76,"text":"Second, they should go to regular checkups."},{"start":243.5,"end":246.04,"text":"Remember, glaucoma is often quiet."},{"start":246.68,"end":249.02,"text":"The patient may not notice if things get worse."},{"start":249.46,"end":250.4,"text":"The doctor can."},{"start":250.76,"end":251.92,"text":"This can be hard."},{"start":252.56,"end":257.76,"text":"Using drops every day for years takes effort, especially when your eyes feel normal."},{"start":258.56,"end":260.42,"text":"But this is exactly the point."},{"start":261.08,"end":264.14,"text":"You are not treating how your eyes feel today."},{"start":264.96,"end":268.48,"text":"You are protecting the sight you will need for the rest of your life."}],"words":[{"text":"Imagine","start":0,"end":0.34},{"text":"some","start":0.34,"end":0.64},{"text":"people","start":0.64,"end":0.86},{"text":"at","start":0.86,"end":1.02},{"text":"an","start":1.02,"end":1.16},{"text":"eye","start":1.16,"end":1.3},{"text":"test","start":1.3,"end":1.64},{"text":"They","start":2.18,"end":2.26},{"text":"all","start":2.26,"end":2.4},{"text":"feel","start":2.4,"end":2.58},{"text":"fine","start":2.58,"end":2.94},{"text":"They","start":3.48,"end":3.6},{"text":"can","start":3.6,"end":3.76},{"text":"see","start":3.76,"end":3.96},{"text":"well","